</region>
<region region-id="267" left="18.00" top="5750.31" width="572.00" height="38.50" align-x="18.00" align-y="5758.81" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Note" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Figure 3. Demand/capacity ratio of each distilled check (stems) against the limit (dashed line). It is a Mathcad plot of CheckGood and CheckNoGood, so it recalculates with the worksheet and a check turns red when its ratio passes 1.0.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="268" left="18.00" top="5796.81" width="572.00" height="27.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="5805.31" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Note" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Check numbers: 1 local buckling D/t; 2 KL/r; 3 axial compression; 4 axial + flexure, 6.9.2.2.1; 5 shear; 6 tension; 7 pile spacing.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="269" left="0" top="5826.81" width="6000" height="6" align-x="0" align-y="5826.81" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<pageBreak/>
</region>
<region region-id="270" left="18.00" top="5838.81" width="572.00" height="73.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="5847.31" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Note" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">The notebook lists 16 PENDING items; the distilled ratios below do not close them: Local buckling class · nonslender (D/t vs 0.11 E/Fy); Slenderness KL/r ≤ 120; Axial compression · maximum Pu / φc Pn; Combined axial load and flexure · Eq. 6.9.2.2.1 (-1); Shear · round tube; Tension · maximum strength uplift; Pile Data Table completeness (SDM 11.4); Steel grade and Fy reconciled; Corrosion allowance; Environment classification; Pile-to-cap connection (12 in embedment); Downdrag source documented; FBMP export current; Minimum tip elevation; Scour resistance and elevations; Drivability.</p></text>
</region>
